From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: let the DSU follow the CPU policies

What. A `dsu` node for the DSU devfreq driver -- the CPU CCU's DSU mux as
its clock and the DSU's AXI divider as "axi", DCDC5 as its supply, the CPU speed-bin cell -- and the vendor's
DSU operating-point table for every speed bin it describes: eleven points
from 312 to 1274 MHz, one opp-microvolt-speed<bin> per bin and an unnamed
worst-case voltage.

Ported from: Allwinner BSP configs/linux-6.6/sun60iw2p1-cpu-vf.dtsi,
dsu_opp_table, radxa/allwinner-bsp aiot-linux-v1.4.8 (e1524a9d),
identical in cubie-aiot-v1.5.0 (c83016d2) and in the linux-6.18 copy.
Generated from that file, not typed: the 26 MHz column family
(opp-microvolt-26m-vfXXXX), because the DSU PLL is fed by the 26 MHz DCXO
(UM V1.00 table 4-2, page 20: reference clock 26 MHz).

Column to bin, the bin being the raw fuse value (bits 15:8 of SID 0x4c)
as in the CPU tables: vf0100..vf0600 -> speed1..speed6, vf0401 -> speed20
(fuse 0x14), vf0501 -> speed21 (0x15), per the vendor's vf_mapping_table.

Where the vendor table differs or is incomplete, and what this one does:
  - vf_mapping_table maps fuse 0x11 and 0x12 to vf0101 and vf0201, but the
    DSU table has no such columns. Those parts get the worst case here
    instead of whatever the vendor's parser falls back to.
  - vf0000 is the column for a zero fuse. A zero fuse and a bin-0 part are
    indistinguishable, so it is not carried (the worst case covers both);
    that drops 546, 1196 and 1352 MHz, which only vf0000 lists.
  - No worst-case column at all. Here: the highest voltage any column gives,
    on the five points every carried column lists (312, 598, 780, 910,
    1066 MHz: 800, 800, 800, 850, 950 mV), marked by BIT(0).
  - The vendor driver binds a "dsu" OPP regulator (the board DT sets
    dsu-supply) but only ever sets the clock, so no voltage is voted. Here
    the OPP core votes it, and the driver caps the DSU at the A55's voltage.
  - The vendor node's clock is the DSU PLL, and the CPU CCU's DSU mux parent
    list does not match the UM (pll-peri0-2x/pll-cpu-back where UM 5.1.10.37, page 310,
    says CPU0PLL/PERI0_600M). Here the clock is our CPU CCU's DSU mux.
  - clock-latency-ns (244144) is not carried: the governor does not use it.

Also corrects the cluster0 table's comment, which still said the DSU runs
at a fixed 780 MHz with no DT representation.

Checked against the UM: every point is a multiple of 26 MHz; points below
650 MHz (312, 598) are reached through EXT_DIVP (CPU_DSU_PLL_CLK_REG[17:16],
/2 or /4, UM 5.1.10.37 page 310) with the VCO inside 650 MHz..2.26 GHz
(UM table 4-2 page 20; CPU_DSU_PLL_CTRL_REG N field, 5.1.10.30 pages 304-305),
which the CPU CCU's rate search picks: 312 = 26 x 48 / 4, 598 = 26 x 46 / 2.
Voltages are multiples of 10 mV inside DCDC5's window and at or below its
regulator-max of 1050 mV.

Only bins 4 and 5 are selectable today (the CPU tables describe no other);
the other columns are carried from the vendor and not silicon-verified.

Verified: the dtb of a test build carries the 11 points, speed4 at
1066 MHz = 840 mV, 1274 MHz supported-hw 0x300034. On the 6 GiB board
(bin 4) devfreq lists exactly the bin-4 column (312-1274 MHz, 9 points),
and every case of the driver's policy proof lands on that column's point
and voltage.

Assisted-by: Claude
---

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -3366,9 +3366,9 @@
 	 * `nvmem-cpufreq-a733-speed-bin-from-efuse` ANDs the per-CPU masks.
 	 *
 	 * DCDC5 is one rail feeding VDD-CPUL and VDD-DSU together, so
-	 * these are also the DSU's voltages. The DSU runs at a fixed
-	 * 780 MHz and has no DT representation; the lowest entry here is
-	 * 800 mV, which is what it is measurably running on today.
+	 * these are also the DSU's voltages: the DSU driver caps the DSU
+	 * at the highest point this table's current voltage covers
+	 * (dsu_opp_table below).
 	 */
 	cluster0_opp: opp-table-cluster0 {
 		compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-operating-points";
@@ -3690,6 +3690,169 @@
 		};
 
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The DSU (L3 + snoop filter) and its per-bin voltage table.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor's table (Allwinner BSP sun60iw2p1-cpu-vf.dtsi, dsu_opp_table),
+	 * 26 MHz column family: the DSU PLL is DCXO-fed. One named voltage per
+	 * speed bin, opp-microvolt-speed<bin>, with <bin> the raw fuse value as
+	 * in the CPU tables: vf0100..vf0600 -> speed1..speed6, vf0401 -> speed20
+	 * (fuse 0x14), vf0501 -> speed21 (0x15). Not carried: vf0000, because a
+	 * zero fuse and a bin-0 part cannot be told apart (the worst case covers
+	 * both), which drops the three points only vf0000 lists (546, 1196 and
+	 * 1352 MHz); and vf0101/vf0201 (fuse 0x11/0x12), for which the vendor's
+	 * DSU table has no column, so those parts take the worst case. The
+	 * driver selects a column only for a bin the CPU tables describe too.
+	 *
+	 * The unnamed opp-microvolt is the worst case, the highest voltage any
+	 * column gives, on the points every carried column lists; BIT(0) marks
+	 * them. The driver never lets the DSU ask for more than the A55 cluster
+	 * already holds on the shared rail (DCDC5; that it also feeds the DSU is
+	 * the vendor DT's dsu-supply, only a hint),
+	 * so the points above the A55's highest voltage are listed but not
+	 * reached. Values below 650 MHz run the PLL at twice or four times the
+	 * rate behind EXT_DIVP (UM 5.1.10.37), inside the 650 MHz..2.26 GHz VCO
+	 * window (UM table 4-2).
+	 */
+	dsu_opp_table: opp-table-dsu {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+
+		opp-312000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <312000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed3 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed6 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x0030007f>;
+		};
+
+		opp-598000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <598000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed3 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed6 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x0030007f>;
+		};
+
+		opp-780000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <780000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed3 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed6 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x0030007f>;
+		};
+
+		opp-832000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <832000000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x00000002>;
+		};
+
+		opp-910000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <910000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <850000 850000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <850000 850000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed3 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed6 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x0030007f>;
+		};
+
+		opp-988000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <988000000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <900000 900000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x00000006>;
+		};
+
+		opp-1066000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1066000000>;
+			opp-microvolt = <950000 950000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <950000 950000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <850000 850000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed3 = <860000 860000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <840000 840000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed6 = <840000 840000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <800000 800000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x0030007f>;
+		};
+
+		opp-1144000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1144000000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <1000000 1000000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <900000 900000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <880000 880000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <820000 820000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <820000 820000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <820000 820000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x00300036>;
+		};
+
+		opp-1222000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1222000000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed1 = <1050000 1050000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <950000 950000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <920000 920000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <860000 860000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <860000 860000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <840000 840000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x00300036>;
+		};
+
+		opp-1248000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1248000000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <1000000 1000000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <960000 960000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <900000 900000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <900000 900000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <860000 860000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x00300034>;
+		};
+
+		opp-1274000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1274000000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed2 = <1050000 1050000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed4 = <1000000 1000000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed5 = <950000 950000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed20 = <950000 950000 1050000>;
+			opp-microvolt-speed21 = <900000 900000 1050000>;
+			opp-supported-hw = <0x00300034>;
+		};
+	};
+
+	dsu {
+		compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-dsu";
+		clocks = <&cpupll_ccu CLK_CPU_DSU>, <&cpupll_ccu CLK_CPU_DSU_AXI>;
+		clock-names = "dsu", "axi";
+		operating-points-v2 = <&dsu_opp_table>;
+		dsu-supply = <&reg_dcdc5>;
+		nvmem-cells = <&cpu_speed_grade>;
+		nvmem-cell-names = "speed";
+	};
 };
 
